<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gjon Marka Gjoni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1888–<a href="/years/1966">1966</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Gjon Markagjoni</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gjon <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marka">Marka</a> Gjoni was the hereditary captain of the Catholic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirdita">Mirdita</a> clan region of northern Albania. Opposed to the new government in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tirana">Tirana</a>, he proclaimed the Republic of Mirdita in July 1921 with backing from the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a>. The republic collapsed within months when Albanian government forces moved in, and he fled to Yugoslavia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gjon-marka-gjoni.jpg" alt="Gjon Marka Gjoni" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kel Marubi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gjon_Marka_Gjoni.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
